  "result": "Quiz 0002 is written to `quizzes/0002.json`, with its key in `keys/0002.json`. It has six items on O4, and every item carries the id O4.\n\n- **Items:** four multiple choice, one short answer and one numeric.\n- **Coverage:** the first four items test who owns the control flow, including a routing case where the model only labels the message. The last two test when a fixed workflow is the better choice. One of those is a cost calculation for your model budget. The other asks which makerspace request needs an agent.\n- **Order:** the quiz moves from the basic definition to applying it in your makerspace assistant.\n- **Ahead of the lessons:** no lesson covers this objective yet. I built the quiz from the objective's wording alone, without a web source, so treat it as a check of where you stand, not a review.\n- **Misconception ids:** I left `distractors` out of the key on purpose. The workspace's existing misconception ids (M1–M6) don't map cleanly onto these wrong answers, and I didn't want to invent new ones.\n\nDo you want a lesson on workflows versus agents before you take it, or would you rather try the quiz cold first?",
